{
  "id": "046",
  "title": "Dungeon and Breakfast",
  "subtitle": "\"I woke up as a dungeon core in the basement of a retired farmer. The System said I was supposed to kill and eat adventurers. I opened a bed-and-breakfast instead.\"",
  "penName": "Hollowell Vine",
  "genre": "dungeonTower",
  "hook": "I was a dungeon core. The System installed me in the basement of Old Barnaby Finn's farmhouse on a Tuesday. The System's welcome notification said I should lure adventurers down, kill them, absorb their mana, and level my floors. I thought about this for four hours. I did not agree. I spawned my first monster — a confused house goblin — and asked her to help me design a welcome mat. Six weeks later I had three floors, two goblins, one minotaur who preferred gardening to guarding, and a laminated menu at the entrance.",
